From 00c6a9895c5e1afe351ac10ec62bde9c50945169 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 3 Sep 2026 22:46:34 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Texture filtering: RDP-exact 3-point, JINC2 mode
 (DuckStation's), live texfilter A/B field

3-point is now the N64 RDP datapath as angrylion-rdp-plus tex.c has it:
10.5 coordinates with 5-bit fractions, upper = (sfrac + tfrac) & 0x20,
the integer lerps with +0x10 >> 5 rounding on 5->8 bit-replicated
channels. s = u - 0.5 maps the N64's centre-at-integer texel to the
PS1's point-sampled cell. Coverage and STP are filtered as channels and
the colour renormalised (DuckStation's premultiplied rule); cutout
authority stays with the containing texel as in the bilinear path.

texture_filtering = "jinc2" (mode 4): Hyllian's windowed-jinc 2-lobe
sharper with anti-ringing, as DuckStation ships it (4x4 taps, wa/wb
constants, AR 0.8), same coverage/STP handling. game.toml [video] accepts
every mode; the F1 Texture filtering choice maps to Nearest / Bilinear /
3-Point / JINC2 instead of collapsing the mode to a nearest/linear bool.
{"cmd":"pgxp","texfilter":N} switches the mode live and the reply
reports it.
